          "title": "You'll want to know: すいそくする",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "すいそくする — suisoku suru — \"to guess; to conjecture\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "もし まよったら、すいそくしないで ください。 — moshi mayottara, suisokushinaide kudasai — \"If you are unsure, please do not guess.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite すいそくします, suisokushimasu; a する verb. Past (polite): せんせいが こたえを すいそくしました。, sensei ga kotae o suisokushimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "すいそくする (suisoku suru) is the Sino-Japanese (kango) noun suisoku with the native verb suru, \"to do\": two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are sui, \"conjecture\" (Middle Chinese tsyhwij) and soku, \"fathom\" (tsrhik) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
